id: pm-brand-identity
title: Accept approved author and committer identities with a trusted forward baseline
description: "Mirror fleet identity controls, diagnose offending commits and roles, and exercise real adversarial Git histories. Release remains held."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T09:26:07.924Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T05:07:44.325Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-brand-kit
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:26:12.086Z",codex-agent,"Design: approved public emails, not display names; audit author and committer on every reachable commit after the root anchor. Read controls from the trusted default branch after adoption so a PR cannot widen its own allow-list or advance its own baseline. Keep the existing tracked UTF-8 path gate and the release hold."
  "2026-10-17T09:28:15.594Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: replacing only scripts/identity.ts with origin/main leaves the new tests unchanged and fails 6 of 7 cases, including approved fleet identities and missing-base refusal. Restoring the implementation passes 7 of 7. Typecheck and docstring gates pass. No tags, publishing or release activation."
  "2026-10-17T09:31:57.200Z",codex-agent,"Validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed in CI identity environments. Each ran 47 tests with 47 passes, zero failures or skips; all source statements, branches, functions and lines are 100%. Both packed npm and Bun consumer acceptances passed. Linked adversarial tests also passed 7/7. The root anchor covers every later kit and merge commit. Release remains held."
  "2026-10-17T12:17:51.723Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 review: fail closed for absent trusted controls; validate proposed controls without activating them; audit both reachable histories with exact emails; isolate merge-committer regression; pin trusted base SHA. Main currently has neither control, so adoption must remain blocked until independently trusted controls exist. Main protection already requires strict verify (22), verify (26), and analyze checks."
  "2026-10-17T12:24:03.816Z",codex-agent,"All six independent behavioral reverts were caught by unchanged real-Git regressions (one failure each): untrusted control fallback, skipped proposed-control validation, omitted base-only history, ignored stale pinned base, trimmed oldest committer email, and skipped merge identities. The restored identity suite passes 14/14. CodeRabbit replacement/removal of both controls is covered. npm and Bun release:check both fail closed because main has neither trusted control; no bypass or ref rewrite is used. Existing strict required checks with admin enforcement were verified through the GitHub protection API."
  "2026-10-17T12:31:30.011Z",codex-agent,"Final Round 1 validation: the real-Git suite passes 14/14, including a policy revocation between checks; the linked six-revert script passes with every mutation caught. Missing origin/main fails even when a local main exists. Downstream checks run separately pass 54/54 tests, zero failures/skips, 100/100/100/100 source coverage, typecheck, lint, build parity, docstrings, font/assets budgets, production audit, 77 intended packed files, and packed npm/Bun consumers. Full npm and Bun release:check both remain blocked at identity:check because trusted main controls are absent. Independent adoption on main is required; release remains held."
  "2026-10-18T03:00:28.414Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: independently adopt the exact email-list and forward-baseline controls in a separate main-based bootstrap PR. Keep trusted-base policy evaluation and add a committed dual-control-edit regression. Full gates remain blocked until the orchestrator merges bootstrap and refreshes this branch; release stays held."
  "2026-10-18T03:07:49.749Z",codex-agent,"Issue 3 root cause confirmed: old main audits all historical display names and already allows Dependabot. The controls-only bootstrap anchors current main; PR 4 then uses independently adopted emails for both author and committer only after that anchor. Added a legacy squash plus dependency regression with a new-unknown-identity negative control and a forward-baseline behavioral revert. Bootstrap itself remains red under the unchanged old gate."
  "2026-10-18T03:12:12.692Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 regression evidence: 16/16 real-Git tests pass, including committed edits to both controls and inherited squash/dependency history. Eight independent safeguard reverts are caught (one failing regression each). The controls-only bootstrap is PR 6 at 993008556c26cf60828d2c928bf54b19c8750e7c and its unchanged old identity gate is red on inherited main history. PR 4 and PR 5 remain fail-closed until independent controls are on main."
  "2026-10-18T04:52:30.297Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: bootstrap PR #6 is independently adopted on main. Retain the trusted-base gate while integrating main; verify the exact adopted controls and both release gates, then push without merging. Release remains held."
  "2026-10-18T05:01:23.081Z",codex-agent,"Main bootstrap controls match both adopted files byte for byte; the trusted-base gate reads them from main commit 98cbe45976b3111f09143c2a29ede906cb553c2a. The 16-test identity suite and eight independent safeguard reverts pass. The npm release gate passes 56/56 tests and 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. The first Bun attempt exposed global extension host-version skew, so repeat it under the same isolated CI home as npm."
  "2026-10-18T05:07:27.616Z",codex-agent,"Ready for CI after merging main: npm release:check passed 56/56 tests with 100/100/100/100 source coverage and packed npm/Bun acceptance. The unchanged trusted-base implementation now reads independently adopted controls from main. Eight behavioral reverts and 16 real-Git regressions pass. Isolated Bun validation is running; exact-head Node 22/26 CI must confirm before orchestration. Release remains held; PRs remain unmerged."
